                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A Rhenish wine, of a light yellow color, either sparkling or still, from the Hochheim region; often applied to all Rhenish wines."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e0f573e0-f5e8-416d-874f-92c4e9d101b6",
                                                "sense_id": "c9c1336f-88a1-3924-8a01-adc7d3be3ad2",
                                                "text": "That night he strolled into the Palette Club about eleven o’clock, and found Trevor sitting by himself in the smoking-room drinking hock and seltzer."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bbc42d4f-8bb2-4c92-8dec-ee9d6795641f",
                                                "sense_id": "c9c1336f-88a1-3924-8a01-adc7d3be3ad2",
                                                "text": "The dinner that they sat down to in the fly-specked dining-room was of boiled beef and carrots, with a turgid ginger pudding to follow, though Grierson went down to the cellar himself and found some dusty bottles of hock, overlooked for years because there was no demand for it in a beer-drinking community."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
